SUMMARY:Russell Peters LIVE at Pittsburgh Improv
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout Russell Peters\nRussell Peters is one of the most celebrated stand-up comedians in the world\, recently named by Rolling Stone as one of the 50 Best Comics of All Time. \nThe Toronto-born comedian started doing stand-up at age 19 and spent 15 years honing his craft before his 2004 CTV special launched him to global stardom. He became the first comedian to sell out Toronto’s Air Canada Centre and went on to break attendance records at Madison Square Garden\, the Sydney Opera House\, and London’s O2 Arena. \nIn 2013\, Peters became the first comedian to create a Netflix Original Comedy Special. His Relax* World Tour (*It’s not that serious.) brings his signature observational humor and crowd work to stages across North America. \nEvent Details\nDate: Thursday\, August 6\, 2026\nTime: 7:00 PM (doors open at 6:00 PM)\nVenue: Pittsburgh Improv\, 166 E. Bridge St\, Homestead\, PA 15120\nTour: Relax* World Tour (*It’s not that serious.)\nAge Restriction: 21+ Event\nShow Duration: Approximately 90 minutes \nAbout the Venue\nThe Pittsburgh Improv is Pittsburgh’s premier comedy club\, located in the Waterfront entertainment complex in Homestead\, PA — just minutes from downtown Pittsburgh. \nThe intimate showroom seats approximately 300 guests with excellent sightlines from every seat. A full-service bar and restaurant are on-site\, with a two-drink minimum per person. \nFree parking is available throughout the Waterfront complex. Easily accessible via I-376 and Route 837. Arrive early to enjoy dinner before the show. \nWhat to Expect\nRussell Peters is famous for his razor-sharp crowd work and his ability to turn any audience member into comedy gold. No two shows are ever the same. \nExpect hilarious observations about culture\, race\, family\, and everyday life delivered with world-class timing. His ability to connect with diverse audiences has made him one of the most beloved live performers in comedy history. \nThe Pittsburgh Improv typically features a local opener before the headliner takes the stage. \nTicket Information\nTickets range from $30 – $75 depending on seating and availability. \nOfficial TicketsResale Tickets \nThis post contains affiliate links. We may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
URL:https://comedycalendar.com/event/russell-peters-live-at-pittsburgh-improv/
LOCATION:Pittsburgh Improv\, 166 E. Bridge St\, Homestead\, Pennsylvania\, 15120\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://s1.ticketm.net/dam/a/7cc/5822d04f-2a7b-4279-a63a-1fe32c3107cc_RETINA_PORTRAIT_3_2.jpg
GEO:40.4089383;-79.9149412
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Pittsburgh Improv 166 E. Bridge St Homestead Pennsylvania 15120 United States;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=166 E. Bridge St:geo:-79.9149412,40.4089383
END:VEVENT
